{"type":"new","contents":"import InfoGeometry.Basic\nimport InfoGeometry.Canonical.FierzReadout\nimport InfoGeometry.Meta.Architecture\nimport Mathlib.Algebra.Lie.OfAssociative\n\n/-!\n# InfoGeometry.Canonical.OperatorialFierzDerivationBridge\n\nConstructive bridge for operatorial Fierz inner derivations.\n\nThis file formalizes only a narrow algebraic readout: spatial-derivative language\nis represented by inner derivations `[K, ·]` on an observable algebra, and the\nGrade-1 Fierz piece of a spinorial product supplies one such inner derivation.\n\nIt does not prove a thermodynamic-gravity equivalence or a spacetime-existence\ntheorem.  The exported predicate below is a derivation matching predicate: it\nidentifies a modular inner derivation with the Grade-1 Fierz inner derivation.\n-/\n\nopen InfoGeometry.Canonical.FierzReadout\n\nnamespace InfoGeometry.Canonical.OperatorialFierz\n\nvariable {𝒜 : Type*} [NormedRing 𝒜] [NormedAlgebra ℝ 𝒜] [StarRing 𝒜]\n\n/--\nNoncommutative operator derivation on the observable algebra.\n\nThis is the owner surface used in the operatorial Fierz bridge: the algebra is\nnot assumed commutative, so we package the Leibniz rule explicitly instead of\nforcing Mathlib's commutative `Derivation` type.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nstructure OperatorDerivation (𝒜 : Type*) [Add 𝒜] [SMul ℝ 𝒜] [Mul 𝒜] where\n  toFun : 𝒜 → 𝒜\n  map_add' : ∀ X Y, toFun (X + Y) = toFun X + toFun Y\n  map_smul' : ∀ (r : ℝ) X, toFun (r • X) = r • toFun X\n  leibniz' : ∀ X Y, toFun (X * Y) = toFun X * Y + X * toFun Y\n\ninstance {𝒜 : Type*} [Add 𝒜] [SMul ℝ 𝒜] [Mul 𝒜] :\n    CoeFun (OperatorDerivation 𝒜) (fun _ => 𝒜 → 𝒜) :=\n  ⟨OperatorDerivation.toFun⟩\n\n/--\nInner derivation generated by an operator `A`: `δ_A(X) = [A, X]`.\n\nThis replaces the classical coordinate-based derivative.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ndef innerDerivation (A : 𝒜) : OperatorDerivation 𝒜 where\n  toFun := fun X => A * X - X * A\n  map_add' := fun X Y => by\n    simp only [mul_add, add_mul]\n    abel\n  map_smul' := fun r X => by\n    simp only [Algebra.mul_smul_comm, Algebra.smul_mul_assoc, smul_sub]\n  leibniz' := fun X Y => by\n    simp only [mul_add, add_mul, mul_assoc, sub_eq_add_neg, neg_mul, mul_neg]\n    -- After expansion: AXY + -(XYA) = (AXY + -(XAY)) + (XAY + -(XYA))\n    -- This is a simple additive identity.\n    abel\n\n/--\nGrade-1 (Vector) projection of an operator.\nIn a physical spacetime model, this extracts the translational generator.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nstructure FierzGradeProjections (𝒜 : Type*) [Add 𝒜] [SMul ℝ 𝒜] where\n  grade1 : 𝒜 → 𝒜\n  is_linear : ∀ (r : ℝ) (A B : 𝒜), grade1 (r • A + B) = r • grade1 A + grade1 B\n\n/--\nGrade-1 Fierz inner derivation generated by the Grade-1 piece of two spinorial\noperators `Ψ` and `Φ`.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ndef fierzGrade1InnerDerivation\n    (P : FierzGradeProjections 𝒜) (Ψ Φ : 𝒜) : OperatorDerivation 𝒜 :=\n  innerDerivation (P.grade1 (Ψ * star Φ))\n\n/--\nPredicate identifying the modular inner derivation with the Grade-1 Fierz inner\nderivation.  This is a matching predicate, not an equivalence of presentations\nand not a spacetime-existence theorem.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ndef ModularFlowMatchesFierzGrade1Derivation\n    (K_mod : 𝒜) (P : FierzGradeProjections 𝒜) (Ψ Φ : 𝒜) : Prop :=\n  innerDerivation K_mod = fierzGrade1InnerDerivation P Ψ Φ\n\n/--\nThe Grade-1 Fierz inner derivation satisfies the Leibniz rule because it is an\ninner derivation generated by `P.grade1 (Ψ * star Φ)`.\n-/\ntheorem fierzGrade1InnerDerivation_leibniz\n    (P : FierzGradeProjections 𝒜) (Ψ Φ : 𝒜) :\n    ∀ (X Y : 𝒜),\n      (fierzGrade1InnerDerivation P Ψ Φ) (X * Y) =\n      (fierzGrade1InnerDerivation P Ψ Φ) X * Y +\n        X * (fierzGrade1InnerDerivation P Ψ Φ) Y :=\n  fun X Y => (fierzGrade1InnerDerivation P Ψ Φ).leibniz' X Y\n\nend InfoGeometry.Canonical.OperatorialFierz\n","mtime":1778188385660}